// ============================================================================
// NOTES
// ============================================================================
/*
Best Practices:
1. Always include count and timestamp (minimum)
2. Calculate rate if possible (helps TipsyHomeLab)
3. Use QoS 1 for reliability
4. Retain messages so new subscribers get latest state
5. Include sensor_id if multiple sensors
6. Report errors rather than failing silently
7. Keep messages small (< 1KB)
8. Publish at reasonable intervals (not every millisecond!)

Common Issues:
- Timestamp in wrong format (must be milliseconds, not seconds)
- Missing required fields (count, timestamp)
- Invalid JSON formatting
- Rate calculated incorrectly (should be bubbles/minute)
- Publishing too frequently (overwhelms broker)

Testing:
1. Publish test message via mosquitto_pub
2. Subscribe to verify message received
3. Check Home Assistant entity updates
4. Monitor logs for errors
5. Verify data in history graph
*/
